      "notes": "Opening epithet must parallel later day-openers: a primal, pre-institutional designation of the Father as the first principle “dwelling” in the midst of the aeons. “first-born” fits the substrate idiom for the primal source without later ecclesial framing; “who dwells a-” anticipates “midst the aeons…”.",
